{
  "_comment": [
    "seti-cookbook MCP companion - OPTIONAL, OFF BY DEFAULT.",
    "This file is deliberately named .mcp.json.example so that nothing starts",
    "automatically. To enable it: `cp .mcp.json.example .mcp.json` (Claude Code",
    "picks up .mcp.json at the repo root), or paste the seti-cookbook block into your",
    "own client config. Requires `pip install fastmcp`.",
    "It is a LOCAL stdio process. It opens no port and sends nothing anywhere",
    "itself; see the MCP section of the README for the full privacy statement.",
    "SETI_COOKBOOK_MCP_ALLOW_ANY_PATH=1 lifts the repo-only filesystem sandbox.",
    "Use the interpreter that has this repo's requirements installed (blimpy /",
    "h5py / hdf5plugin), which is often a conda env rather than bare `python`."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "seti-cookbook": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["tools/seti_cookbook_mcp.py"],
      "env": {
        "SETI_COOKBOOK_GPU": "0"
      }
    }
  }
}
